  "question": {
    "text": "The initial volume of a gas cylinder is $750.0 \\mathrm{~mL}$. If the pressure of gas inside the cylinder changes from $840.0 \\mathrm{~mm} \\mathrm{Hg}$ to $360.0 \\mathrm{~mm} \\mathrm{Hg}$, the final volume the gas will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$1.750 \\mathrm{~L}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$3.60 \\mathrm{~L}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$4.032 \\mathrm{~L}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$7.50 \\mathrm{~L}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to Boyle's law\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\frac{V_1}{V_2}=\\frac{P_2}{P_1} ; \\frac{750}{V_2}=\\frac{360}{840} \\\\\n&V_2=1750 \\mathrm{ml}=1.750 \\mathrm{~L}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}